    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1092">

                <pb facs="0797" n="681" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg681"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/4058.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Letcher to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Chihuahua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 2, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s May 1. General Carranza has telegraphed urgent orders to General
                    Natera, Constitutionalist military commander in the State of Zacatecas,
                    regarding liberation of Emery should he be held by any of his forces. Zacatecas
                    is still held by Federals. Constitutionalist authorities here are slow to
                    believe that Emery is held by their forces.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Letcher</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
